# supercronic schedule for the `cron` service (TZ=Pacific/Honolulu, cwd /app/web).
# supercronic never starts a job while its previous run is still going.

# Daily refresh at 22:00 HST — matches the old Workflow cron (08:00 UTC): a run
# takes ~90 min and must finish before Banner's ~02:00 HST maintenance window.
# run-daily.sh holds a flock, so it skips (exit 0) if a manual run is still going.
0 22 * * * /app/deploy/home/run-daily.sh

# Nightly backups (VACUUM INTO /data/backups), after the refresh. Local retention
# is BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS (default 14) — lower it when an offsite backup (restic etc.)
# already keeps the history.
0 4 * * * yarn db:backup --dir /data/backups --keepDays "${BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS:-14}"
